$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed coupling of functionalized
aryl chlorides with aliphatic and aromatic thiols. The appropriate
quantity of stock solution A was added to a 4 mL vial containing the aryl
chloride (1.00 mmol) and NaOtBu (230 mg, 2.40 mmol) in 1.5 mL of DME. The
thiol (1.00 mmol) was then added, and the vial sealed with a cap
containing a PTFE septum. The mixture was heated at 110 ºC until the
chloroarene was consumed, as determined by GC. Silica gel (0.5 g) was
added, and the solvents were evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel using hexane
or mixtures of hexane and ethyl acetate as eluent. Aryl sulfides were
isolated in the yields reported in Table 1. 3-Cyanophenyl
2-methyl-2-propyl sulfide (Table 1, entry 20). 50 μL of stock solution A
and NaOtBu (106 mg, 1.10 mmol) were used. 90% yield. White solid. White
solid.1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.82 (s, 1H), 7.76 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.65 (d,
J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.45 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 1.30 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (CDCl3):
δ 141.5, 140.2, 134.7, 132.0, 129.1, 118.1, 112.6, 46.7, 30.8 (3C). Elem.
Anal. Calcd for C11H13NS: C, 69.07; H, 6.85; N, 7.32. Found: C, 69.25; H,
6.78; N, 7.25.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General and Long-Lived Catalyst for the Palladium-Catalyzed Coupling of
Aryl Halides with Thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez-Rodriguez, Manuel A.; Shen, Qilong; Hartwig, John F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(7), 2180-2181

