$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A for Substituted
Benzothiophene-2-carboximindine Analogues (Scheme1).
2-Cyanobenzothiophene (3) Synthesis. To a solution of arylaldehydes (1
equiv) in DMF (3 mL/mmol) and DBU (2 equiv) was added thioacetonitrile
(1.2 equiv) dropwise at 0 °C. The solution was stirred at 0 °C for 20
min, then heated to 40 °C for 16-20 h. The reaction mixture was allowed
cool to room temperature, the solvent was reduced in vacuo, and the
product was purified via silica chromatography (EtOAc/hexane mix),
yielding the intermediates 3.
4-(2-Carbamimidoyl-benzo[b]thiophen-6-yloxymethyl)-benzoic acid methyl
ester hydrochloride (31): Compound was prepared using general procedure A
for amidine synthesis to give 74.2 mg, 90%. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 400 MHz):
9.40 (s, 2 H), 9.02 (s, 2H), 8.32 (s, 1 H), 7.99 (m, 3H), 7.93 (s, 1H),
7.99 (m, 3H), 7.87 (d, J = 2.3 Hz), 7.63 (d, 2H, J = 8.6 Hz), 5.26 (dd,
1H, J = 2.5 8.7 Hz), 5.34 (s, 2H), 3.86 (s, 3H). MS m/z (ES+) 317 [M +
H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, reactant assumed
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Studies of Benzothiophene Template as Potent Factor IXa (FIXa) Inhibitors
in Thrombosis
