$DATUM Bis(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)sulfide 7b: In a sealed tube, a suspension of
4-iodoveratrole (1.10 g, 4.2 mmol), 3,4-dimethoxythiophenol (850 mg, 5
mmol), CuI (76 mg, 0.4 mmol), neocuproine (124 mg, 0.4 mmol), NaOtBu (576
mg, 6 mmol) in toluene (8 ml) was stirred at 110 °C for 3 d under argon
atmosphere. Subsequently, water (10 ml) was added and the mixture was
extracted with dichloromethane (3 x 50 ml). The solution was dried with
magnesium sulfate and the solvents were evaporated. The crude product was
soluted in a minimum of dichloromethane (4 ml) and purified by flash
column chromatography on Al2O3 (alkaline, eluent: cyclohexane/EtOAc, 4:1)
to yield compound 7b. Colorless crystalline solid, yield 1.163 g, 90%. mp
= 92.6 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.94-6.86 (m, 4H), 6.83-6.77 (m,
2H), 3.86 (s, 6H), 3.81 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.41,
148.63, 127.52, 123.96, 114.40, 111.80, 56.08, 56.06. HRMS (ESI+) m/z
calcd for C16H18O4SNa [M+Na]+ 329.0824, found 329.0828.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
