$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Carboxylic Acids 1, 2 (GP 1).
2-(4-Methoxy-2-nitro-phenylsulfanyl)-benzoic acid (1) 2-Mercapto-benzoic
acid (5.00 g, 32.00 mmol) was treated with 1-pentanol (100 mL) and the
mixture heated to reflux (140 °C). 2-Bromo-5-methoxy nitrobenzene (6.49
g, 28.00 mmol) was added to the reaction mixture, followed by K2CO3 (4.01
g, 28.60 mmol) and finally copper powder (155 mg, 2.44 mmol). The mixture
was heated to reflux for 3 h and a solid precipitated. The latter was
filtered off, washed with Et2O (3 × 100 mL) and dried. The brick red
solid was dissolved in water (0.5 L) and the resulting red solution
filtered off from the catalyst. The filtrate was acidified with a 37%
aqueous HCl solution (25 mL) and the resulting precipitate was filtered
off and dried by suction overnight to give benzoic acid 1 (7.83 g, 92%)
as a yellow solid. HPLC: (A) 3.9 min, 90% purity.
2-(4-Chloro-2-nitro-phenylsulfanyl)-benzoic acid (22) The benzoic acid 22
(7.80 g, 90%) was obtained from thiosalicylic acid (5.00 g, 32.00 mmol),
2-bromo-5-chloronitrobenzene (6.68 g, 28.00 mmol) according to GP 1 as a
solid. HPLC: (A) 4.3 min, 90% purity. 1H NMR (200 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ (ppm)
8.26 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.92-7.87 (m, 1H), 7.70 (dd, J = 2.3, 8.6 Hz,
1H), 7.59-7.45 (m, 2H), 7.33-7.29 (m, 1H), 7.20 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H). MS
(APCI), m/z: 309.0 [M+H]+.
