$DATUM 2-Methyl-2-[(4-methyl-2-nitrophenyl)thio]propanoic Acid (22). A catalytic
amount of TBAB (5-10% w/w) was added to a stirred solution of
4-chloro-3-nitrotoluene (3.00 g, 2.31 mL, 17.48 mmol) in dry DMSO (10 mL)
heated at 100 °C. After 5 min, Cs2CO3 (17.10 g, 52.48 mmol) and
2-mercapto-2-methylpropanoic acid40 (4.19 g, 34.87 mmol) were added.
After 2 h, the mixture was cooled, poured into ice-water, washed with
EtOAc, acidified to pH 2 with 12 N HCl, and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried, and evaporated to
dryness. The residue was treated with water, filtered off, and dried. 22
(4.03 g, 90%) as a yellow ochre solid which was used in the next step
without further purification. Mp 100-102 °C, 1H NMR (200 MHz) δ 1.50 (6H,
s, CH3), 2.45 (3H, s, ArCH3), 7.35 (1H, ddd, J = 0.7, 1.9, 8.0 Hz, H-5),
7.55 (1H, d, J = 8.0, H-6), 7.60 (1H, dd, J = 0.7, 1.9 Hz, H-3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
