$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Route C. Preparation of 3-(Ethylthio)-2-fluoro-6-nitrophenol (16). To a
suspension of sodium ethanethiolate (5.00 g, 2.83 equiv, 47.6 mmol) in
tetrahydrofuran (25 mL) at 0 °C, under a nitrogen atmosphere was added a
solution of 2,3-difluoro-6- nitrophenol (15) (3.00 g, 1.00 equiv, 16.8
mmol) in tetrahydrofuran (25 mL) over 5 min to give a brown slurry. The
mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture was then
partitioned between ethyl acetate (50 mL), aqueous hydrochloric acid (1
M, 50 mL) and aqueous sodium chloride solution (saturated, 50 mL). The
layers were separated, and the organic layer was washed with aqueous
sodium chloride solution (saturated, 2 × 15 mL), dried over magnesium
sulfate, and filtered, and the solvent was removed in vacuo, affording a
brown solid, which was purified by flash column chromatography (eluent
10% EtOAc in isohexane) affording 3-(ethylthio)- 2-fluoro-6-nitrophenol
(16) as an orange oil (2.05 g). 3-(ethylthio)- 2-fluoro-6-nitrophenol
(16), yield 90%. GC purity 90%; tR 14.5 min; mp (crude) 70.5-71.5 °C;
υmax cm-1 3231, 1512, 1204, 1143; δH (400 MHz, d6-DMSO) 1.29 (t, J = 7.3
Hz, 3H), 3.11 (q, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 7.00 (dd, J = 6.9, 9.2 Hz, 1H), 7.79
(dd, J = 1.8, 9.2 Hz, 1H), 11.14 (s, 1H); δC (100 MHz, d6-DMSO) 13.78,
24.42, 115.50, 120.54 (d, J = 3.1 Hz), 133.68 (d, J = 14.6 Hz), 134.76
(d, J = 3.1 Hz), 141.26 (d, J = 16.9 Hz), 148.24 (d, J = 239.4 Hz); MS
(EI+) 217 (M+).
