$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Synthesis of
4-Methoxyphenyl Phenyl Sulfide (Table 2, entry 2). An oven-dried 4 mL
vial containing a stirrer bar was charged with an 4-methoxyphenyl bromide
(93.5 mg, 0.5 mmol), catalyst (6.5 mg, 2 mol%) and KOtBu (84.2 mg, 0.75
mmol) in the glove box and sealed with a cap containing a PTFE / Silicone
septum. Toluene (1 mL) and thiophenyl (0.60 mmol) were injected
sequentially. The mixture was stirred at 100°C for 6 h. The crude was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel with petroleum ether as
eluent. 1-(4-(Benzylthio)phenyl)ethanol (Table 3, entry 6): silica gel
column chromatography (petroleum ether/ether 10:3) gave 109.9 mg (0.45
mmol, 90%) of the product as white solid. mp 82.1-82.6°C. 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.30-7.25 (m, 9H), 4.88-4.83 (m, 1H), 4.11 (s, 2H), 1.81
(s, 1H), 1.46 (d, J = 6.4Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 144.0,
137.4, 135.3, 129.9, 128.8, 128.5, 127.2, 125.9, 70.0, 39.1, 25.1. Elem.
Anal. Found (calcd for C15H16OS): C 73.94 (73.73), H 6.55 (6.60), N 6.38
(6.55). EIMS m/z: 244 (M+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst prepared and used, the article was retracted by the
corresponding author in "Synlett", 2014, 25(5),750
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
