$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM In the catalytic reactions, to a yellow suspension of 8 (2.0 mg, 3 μmol),
4-fluoroiodobenzene (40 μL, 0.35 mmol) and the appropriate thiol (37 μL,
0.30 mmol) in benzene, was added NaOtBu (33.5 mg, 0.35 mmol) and the
mixture was stirred for 2 h at RT. The progress was monitored by GC. The
orange suspension was filtered and the solution was evaporated. The
residue was purified on a silica gel column to afford the product (from
2-thiocresol). (4-fluorophenyl)(o-tolyl) sulfide, colorless oil, yield
(58.9 mg, 90%). 1H NMR 7.26-7.22 (m, Ar-H, 3H), 7.20-7.10 (m, Ar-H, 3H),
7.02-6.98 (m, Ar-H, 2H), 2.37 (s, CH3, 3H); 13C{1H} 162.17 (d, JFC =
245.9 Hz, C-F), 139.09 (s), 134.91 (s), 132.86 (d, J= 8.1 Hz), 131.74
(s), 130.73 (s), 127.63 (s), 126.86 (s), 116.61 (s), 116.39 (s), 29.86
(s); 19F{1H} -114.48 (s); EI-MS M+ (Calc. for C13H11FS) 218 (218).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Room Temperature Rapid Functionalization of E-H Bonds (E = O, N, S) via
the Metal-Ligand Cooperation Mechanism
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Scharf, Adam; Goldberg, Israel; Vigalok, Arkadi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Inorganic Chemistry (2014), 53(1), 12-14

