$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Anhyd DMSO (5 mL) was added to a mixture of
2-HSC6H4OH (151 mg, 1.2 mmol), 3,4-F2C6H3CN (139 mg, 1.0 mmol), and K2CO3
(345 mg, 2.5 mmol) under N2, and the mixture was stirred for 3 h at 60
°C. The mixture was then cooled to r.t. and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 25
mL). The organic layers were combined, washed with sat. brine (2 × 20
mL), dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography [silica gel,
P-CH2Cl2 (2:1)]. Phenoxathiine-3-carbonitrile (4a), yield: 202 mg (90%),
White solid. m.p. 142.6-143.4 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.98-7.02 (m,
1H), 7.04-7.08 (m, 2H), 7.14-7.20 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.22 (d, 1H, J = 1.5 Hz),
7.25-7.28 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 110.94, 117.97, 120.74,
125.28, 126.77, 127.33, 127.51, 127.98, 128.48, 150.92, 151.94. HRMS
(ESI, m/z): calcd for C13H8NOS [M+H]+ 226.0321, found 226.0334. IR
(film): 753, 822, 883, 1472, 2222 cm-1. Crystal data: Chemical formula:
C13H7NOS, Formula Mass: 225.26, Crystal system: monoclinic, a = 11.960 Å,
b = 6.029 Å, c = 15.117 Å, α = 90.00 °, β = 107.985 °, γ = 90.00°. Space
group: P2(1)/c.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, alternatively reaction carried out at room temperature
increased reaction time and decreased yield, alternative preparation
shown, optimization study, optimized on reagent and solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regioselective synthesis of phenoxathiin derivatives under
transition-metal-free conditions
