$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-((4-nitrophenyl)thio)benzoic acid (2): Thiosalicylic acid (10.0 g, 64.8
mmol) was dissolved in DMF (150 mL) and treated with anhydrous potassium
carbonate (9.3 g, 194.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv.) and the resulting mixture was
stirred for 10 minutes. To the above mixture was added slightly excess of
4-fluoronitrobenzene (11.1 g, 77.9 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) dissolved in 20 mL
of DMF and the reaction was continued at 110 °C for 8 hours till TLC
(EtOAc: petroleum ether, 1:1) showed completion of the reaction. The
reaction mixture was poured into ice-cold water followed by acidification
using 5N HCl leading to the precipitation of crude product. The crude
solid was filtered and washed several times with deionized water and
petroleum ether followed by recrystallization using ethyl alcohol
afforded pure compound 2. Yield (1.60 g, 90%), yellow crystalline solid.
m. p. 224-226 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, Acetone-d6) δ 8.28-8.23 (m, 2H),
8.07-8.03 (m, 1H), 7.66-7.61 (m, 2H), 7.55-7.36 (m, 2H), 7.28-7.25 (dd, J
=7.93, 1.22 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, Acetone-d6) δ 167.52, 146.42,
144.40, 135.22, 132.52, 132.06, 131.90, 131.15, 130.66, 127.40, 124.50.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
