$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Acetic
(N,N-di-o-tolylphosphorothioic)Thioanhydride [(o-MeC6H4O)2PS2C(O)CH3]
(1). For the synthesis of [(o-MeC6H4O)2PS2C(O)CH3], an approximate 20 ml
toluene solution of acetyl chloride, CH3C(O)Cl, (0.43 g, 5.5 mmol) was
added dropwise through dropping funnel into a toluene suspension (∼30 ml)
of sodium salt of O,O'-(o-ditolyl)dithiophosphoric acid,
(o-MeC6H4O)2PS2Na (1.85 g, 5.5 mmol), with constant stirring. The
reaction mixture was refluxed for 15 hours then was brought to room
temperature. The precipitated sodium chloride was removed by filtration
using a funnel fitted with G-4 sintered disc. Subsequently, an excess of
solvent was evaporated under the reduced pressure. Final drying of the
product in vacuo for three hours resulted in the formation of product.
Product: (o-CH3C6H4O)2PS2-o-C6H4CHO, yield: 90%, (Yellow viscous),
Reactants: Ligand: (o-CH3C6H4O)2PS2Na, 1.00 g (3.0 mmol); Organic moiety:
o-ClC6H4CHO, 0.42 g (3.0 mmol). Reflux: 2 h. M.W: found 394.28, calcd
(414.37). Analyses (%), found C 60.80, H 4.39, S 15.40, Calcd. C (60.86),
H (4.58), N (15.48). IR spectrum cm-1 (2922, b, Aromatic ν(C-H)), (1139,
s, ν(P)-O-C)), (897, s, νP-O-(C)), (715, m, νP═S), (562, m, νP-S), (1696,
s, νC═O), (688, m, νC-S). 1H NMR (CDCl3) (δ ppm) 2.3, s, 6H (Ar-CH3)
6.7-6.9, m, 8H (-C6H4); 7.6-7.9, m, 4H (-C6H4);; 10.7, s, 1H (-CHO); 31P
NMR (CDCl3) (δ ppm) 89.3, s. 13C NMR (CDCl3) (δ ppm) Dithio moiety (18.9,
-CH3), (122.1, -C(CH3)), (149.3, P-O-C), (121.4, (C2,6), (128.1, 126.8,
(C3,5), (132.5, C4). Organic moiety (132.3, Cipso), (129.0, 130.2,
Cortho), (135.1, 136.0, Cmeta), (126.9, Cpara), -8.2 (δ'(Cp-Cm)) (190.1,
C═O).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of organoditolyldithiophosphates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gupta, Bhawana; Kumar, Kuldeep; Pandey, Sushil K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis and Reactivity in Inorganic, Metal-Organic, and Nano-Metal
Chemistry (2009), 39(9), 559-565

