$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for palladium-catalyzed
carbon-sulfur bond formation and preparation of compounds 18a, 18b, and
18c. A round-bottomed flask was charged with compound 17a, 17b or 17c
(1.0 eq.), iPr2NEt (2.0 eq.) and dry 1,4-dioxane. The mixture was
evacuated and backfilled with nitrogen (3 cycles). The catalyst Pd2(dba)3
(0.025 eq.), xantphos (0.05 eq.) and 2-ethyl hexyl-3-mercaptopropionate
(1.0 eq.) were added and then the mixture was degassed twice more. The
mixture was heated to reflux for 8 h, after which the completion of the
reaction was confirmed by TLC. Once the reaction was cooled down to room
temperature, it was filtered and concentrated. The crude mixture was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel to afford colorless
sticky liquids as the desired products. For palladium-catalyzed
carbon-sulfur bond formation, compound 17a (0.98 g, 2.0 mmol), iPr2Net
(0.70 mL, 4.0 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (0.04 g, 0.05 mmol), 2-ethyl
hexyl-3-mercaptopropionate (0.45 mL, 2.0 mmol) and xantphos (0.06 g, 0.1
mmol) were employed in dry 1,4-dioxane (5 mL). The compound was purified
over silica gel column using 4:6 hexanes / dichloromethane as an eluent
to obtain the product. For palladium-catalyzed carbon-sulfur bond
formation, compound 17b (0.83 g, 0.90 mmol), iPr2Net (0.32 mL, 1.8 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (0.02 g, 0.02 mmol), 2-ethyl hexyl-3-mercaptopropionate (0.19
mL, 0.90 mmol) and xantphos (0.03 g, 0.04 mmol) were employed in dry
1,4-dioxane (5 mL). The compound was purified over silica gel column
using 6:4 hexanes / ethylacetate as an eluting system to obtain the
product. 2-Ethylhexyl
3-(3-(3,5-bis(3,5-bis(benzyloxy)benzyloxy)benzylthio) phenylthio)
propanoate, yield 0.9 g, 90%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 7.26-7.43 (m,
21H), 7.10-7.16 (m, 3H), 6.66 (s, 4H), 6.56 (s, 4H), 6.47 (s, 1H), 5.03
(s, 8H), 4.92 (s, 4H), 4.00 (s, 2H), 3.98-4.00 (m, 2H), 3.11 (t, J = 7.2
Hz, 2H), 2.58 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.24-1.34 (m, 9H), 0.85-0.88 (m, 6H).
13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 171.8, 160.2, 160.0, 139.5, 139.3, 137.7,
136.9, 136.4, 130.1, 129.4, 128.7, 128.1, 127.7, 127.4, 127.3, 108.0,
106.5, 101.5, 101.3, 70.2, 70.0, 67.3, 39.0, 38.8, 34.4, 30.4, 29.0,
28.9, 23.8, 23.1, 14.2, 11.1. MS(MALDI): m/z 1159.5 (MAg+). Anal. Calcd
for C66H68O8S2: C, 75.25; H, 6.51; O, 12.15; S, 6.09. Found: C, 75.28; H,
6.62; O, 12.33; S, 5.96.
