$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,3,5-Tri(dimethyl-dithiocarbamoyl)-2,4,6-triformylbenzene (2). Aldehyde
1 (2.026 g, 5.080 mmol) was dissolved in acetone (600 mL) and slowly
added to a solution of sodium dithiocarbamate (3.459 g, 20.320 mmol) in
acetone (400 mL) at -80°C. The resulting yellow suspension has been
allowed to warm up to ambient temperature over 15 h and the precipitate
has been removed by filtration. The volatiles of the filtrate have been
removed in vacuum and the resulting solid has been washed several times
with water and dried overnight in an exsiccator. Yield: 2.367g (4.554
mmol, 90%) 1H NMR (500.25 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 10.22 (s, 1H; CHO), 3.50 (s,
3H, CH3), 3.47 (s, 3H, CH3). 13C NMR (125.80 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 191.2 (s,
C=S), 189.1 (s, C=O), 147.5 (s, CArC), 133.2 (s, CArS), 45.8 (s, CH3),
42.7 (s, CH3). ESI MS (positive ion mode) m/z = 520.0 [M+H]+, 542.0
[M+Na]+. IR (KBr) ν ~ / cm-1 = 3443br, 3011w, 2959w, 2926m, 2855w, 1697s,
1504s, 1408w, 1379s, 1244s, 1151s, 1049w, 972s, 860w, 806w, 752s.
Elemental analysis: Found: C, 42.13; H, 4.24; N, 7.89. Calc. for
C18H21N3O3S6·0.2 acetone (C18.6H22.2N3O3.2S6) C, 42.04; H, 4.21, N, 7.91.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, slow addn. of Rubin's trialdehyde (substage 1)
