$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: a. Conjugations with SjGST. A typical reaction
contained 2.85 mL of 20 mM sodium phosphate buffer (pH 7.0), 5 mM reduced
glutathione, and 0.3 μM GST from Schistosoma japonicum (“enzymatic
reaction solution”). The reaction was initiated by adding 150 μL of a 10
mM solution of the electrophile in methanol to the premixed buffer
solution containing GSH and SjGST. The mixture was incubated with
stirring at 25 °C overnight, and then the UV-vis absorption spectrum was
taken at 25 °C. For the reaction mixtures of enzymatic reactions, the
absorbance was intense that a 1:100 dilution of the reaction solution
with phosphate buffer was required to obtain measurements to conform to
Beer’s law (with OD well below 1.0).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM biotransformation, combinatorial, enzymic, SjGST used, sodium phosphate
buffer used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of a Suite of Bioorthogonal Glutathione S-Transferase
Substrates and Their Enzymatic Incorporation for Protein Immobilization
