$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM II. Chemistry-Synthesis and chemical data of intermediates
3-(Methylthio)-4-nitrophenol (6a). To a solution of
3-fluoro-4-nitrophenol (2 g, 12.7 mmol) in dry DMF (67 mL) was added by
aliquots 2 equivalents of sodium thiomethoxide (1.78 g, 25.5 mmol)
followed by 3 equivalents of potassium carbonate (5.27 g, 38.2 mmol). The
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 23 hrs and then water (100
mL) was added. The mixture was extracted with EtOAc, and the combined
organic layers washed successively with water (60 mL) and brine (60 mL)
and then dried over MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated under vacuum to
provide the title compound (2.12 g) as a yellow powder.
3-(Methylthio)-4-nitrophenol (6a)., yield 90% 1H-NMR δ: 2.44 (s, 3H,
HMe), 6.72 (d, 1H, J = 9.0, Harom), 6.79 (s, 1H, Harom), 8.19 (d, 1H, J =
9.1, Harom), 11.20 (bs, 1H, OH). 13C-NMR δ: 15.2, 111.3, 112.0, 128.7,
136.7, 142.0, 162.9.
