$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Solid-phase synthesis of Ac-T(4-thiophenyl-Phe)PN-NH2 (5): Resin with the
4-iodophenylalanine-containing peptide (1') (10-15 mg, 7-10 μmol) was
placed in a glass vial, and toluene (200 μL) and DIPEA (33 μL, 0.2 mmol)
were added. Copper(I) iodide (1.8 mg, 10 μmol); 1,10-phenanthroline (3.6
mg, 20 ymol); and thiophenol (12.3 μL, 0.12 mmol), thiobenzoic acid (14.1
μL, 0.12 mmol), or allyl mercaptan (9.6 μL, 0.12 mmol) were added. The
vial was capped and the mixture was stirred in an oil bath set to 110°C
for 16-18 h. In the case of the peptide 7, the reaction temperature was
set to 100 0°C. The resin was washed with DMF (4 x 4 mL), CH2Cl2 (2 x 4
mL), and MeOH (2 x 4 mL) and dried with ether. The resin was cleaved and
the peptide deprotected under standard cleavage/deprotection conditions
to produce the peptide Ac-T(4-thiophenyl-Phe)PN-NH2 (5). Yield 90%. tR
52.6 min, exp. 626.3, obs. 627.1 (M + H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction, capped vial used, cleavage from resin (stage
2), other products also detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of thiophenylalanine-containing peptides via Cu(I)-mediated
cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Forbes, Christina R.; Zondlo, Neal J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(2), 464-467

