$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Bis(2-(2-(2-ethoxyethoxy)ethoxy)ethylthio)phthalonitrile 5 4, :
2-(2-(2-Methoxyethoxy)ethoxy)ethanethiol (b) (5.6 g, 31.24 mmol) in
anhydrous DMF (5 mL) and finely ground K2CO3 (4.6 g, 33.3 mmol) were
heated up to 70 °C and the mixture stirred at that temperature for 30
min. 4,5 Dichlorophthalonitrile (2.8 g, 14.2 mmol) in anhydrous DMF (6
mL) was added to reaction mixture dropwise. The mixture was stirred for
10 h at 70 °C. The color of the solution was turned from yellow to orange
over the time. After removal of the inorganic salts by filtration, DMF
was evaporated and the crude mixture was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel with EtOAc-hexanes (3:1) mixture as eluting
solvent to give a yellow oil (6.2 g, 90% yield). 1H NMR (250 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 7.9(2H), 3.7(4H), 3.5(12H), 3.4(8H), 3.2(6H); 13C NMR (300
MHz, DMSO- d6) δ143.8, 129.8, 116.9, 110.9, 72.7, 70.6, 70.5, 69.3, 58.9,
32.5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mono-amine Functionalized Phthalocyanines: Microwave-Assisted Solid-Phase
Synthesis and Bioconjugation Strategies
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
