$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General experimental procedures for the
synthesis of Benzo[b]pyrido [2,3-f] [1,4] thiazepin -11(10H)-ones. A 25
mL schlenk tube equipped with a magnetic stiring bar was charged with
halogenous benzenethiol (2a-2e) or
3-chloro-5-(trifluoromethyl)pyridine-2-thiol (5) (0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv),
N-substituted nitrobenzamides (1a-1i) (0.6 mmol, 1.2 equiv), KOH (84 mg,
1.5 mmol, 3.0 equiv) and then 15 mL of DMF or DMSO was added via syringe
at room temperature and the mixture was prestirred for about 15 minutes.
Then the reaction was stirred at 150 °C. After the reaction was
completed, the mixture was diluted with brine (40 mL) and extracted with
ethyl acetate twice (2×30 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
over MgSO4 and the solvent was removed in vacuo to afford a residue. The
crude product was then purified by column chromatography on silica gel to
give the pure product.
6-Chloro-2-nitro-10-propyldibenzo[b,f][1,4]thiazepin-11(10H)-one (3a)
10-(4-Bromophenyl)-6-chloro-2-nitrodibenzo[b,
f][1,4]thiazepin-11(10H)-one (3 g) Brown solid; yield 90%. mp 230-231 °C;
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.64 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 8.20 (dd, J = 2.7,
8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.61-7.56 (m, 2H), 7.34-7.26 (m,
3H), 7.14 (t, J = 8.1, 8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.97 (dd, J = 1.2, 8.1 Hz, 1H).
13CNMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.0, 148.3, 145.3, 145.2, 141.5, 139.4, 137.8,
133.8, 133.0, 132.7, 130.2, 129.8, 128.1, 126.9, 125.6, 121.8. HRMS
(ESI): calcd for C19H10BrClN2O3S (M+ H)+ 460.9357, found 460.9345.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, green chemistry, regioselective, Smiles rearrangement
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One Pot Regioselective Synthesis of a Small Library of
Dibenzo[b,f][1,4]thiazepin-11(10H)-ones via Smiles Rearrangement
