$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step1. Sodium (1.93 g, 84 mmol) was added slowly to 50 mL anhydrous
methanol. After the reaction was complete, benzyl mercaptan E (10.33 g,
83 mmol) in 25 mL anhydrous methanol was added to the solution. The
mixture was stirred at room temperature, and then 2-nitrochlorobenzene D
(13.13 g, 83 mmol) was added dropwise. The reaction was heated under
reflux for 1 h and then cooled overnight. The product precipitated out of
solution, filtered and recrystallized with methanol to give
1-benzylsulfanyl-2-nitro-benzene F Yield (18.39 g, 90.3%), yellow solid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
